div.p:
That for such organization, as well as for moving the troops charged with
                    pursuing the bands which initiated the disturbance of order, extraordinary
                    expenses were incurred and continue to be incurred by the executive;

That to meet these expenditures the receipts fixed by the present estimates have
                    not been sufficient, and it has been necessary to raise funds by private loans,
                    and to divert from their object various special funds;

That in compliance with justice and for the honor of the state the deficit which
                    has resulted in consequence of these exceptional circumstances should be met;
                    and
